<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1905"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 2:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->At 3:00 in the morning and reading this stuff anyone could get creep&#39;d out &#40;accept Tom he says he doesn&#39;t&#41; anyway I saw that one of the names that the Murderer suggested was &#34;Wichita Hangman&#34; This seems an obvious ref. to the Glen Campbell/Jimmy Webb tune &#34;Wichita Lineman.&#34; <BR> <BR>I looked up the lyrics. I&#39;m probably not the first to do so but to my surprise and with a adrenaline rush of creepy 1001 I looked at some other Campbell lyrics and there are many aspects to his hit songs that parallel this case. <BR> <BR>Many singers sing about railroads and playgrounds etc but the Murderer is the one that referred to Wichita Hangman. This guy is a fan of Mr. Campbell and/or this is just plain spooky. <BR> <BR>I know Glen Campbell didn&#39;t write most of his hits but here a few excerpts to consider. What it all means I&#39;m not sure: <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Wichita Lineman&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>I am a lineman for the county and I drive the main road <BR>Searchin&#39; in the sun for another overload <BR>I hear you singin&#39; in the wire, I can hear you through the whine <BR>And the Wichita Lineman is still on the line <BR> <BR>I know I need a small vacation but it don&#39;t look like rain <BR>And if it snows that stretch down south won&#39;t ever stand the strain <BR>And I need you more than want you, and I want you for all time <BR>And the Wichita Lineman is still on the line <BR> <BR>And I need you more than want you, and I want you for all time <BR>And the Wichita Lineman is still on the line <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42; Phone Lines Cut&#42;&#42;&#42; Needs&#42;&#42;&#42; Travel&#42;&#42;&#42; Repairman&#42;&#42;&#42; Searching/&#40;stalking?&#41;&#42;&#42;&#42; &#34;I want you for all time&#34;/Control&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Gentle On My Mind&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>It&#39;s knowin&#39; that your door is always open <BR>And your path is free to walk <BR>That makes me tend to leave my sleepin&#39; bag <BR>Rolled up and stashed behind your couch <BR>And it&#39;s knowin&#39; I&#39;m not shackled <BR>By forgotten words and bonds <BR>And the ink stains that have dried upon some line <BR>That keeps you in the back roads <BR>By the rivers of my memory <BR>That keeps you ever gentle on my mind <BR> <BR>It&#39;s not clingin&#39; to the rocks and ivy <BR>Planted on their columns now that bind me <BR>Or something that somebody said because <BR>They thought we fit together walkin&#39; <BR>It&#39;s just knowing that the world <BR>Will not be cursing or forgiving <BR>When I walk along some railroad track and find <BR>That you&#39;re movin&#39; on the back roads <BR>By the rivers of my memory <BR>And for hours you&#39;re just gentle on my mind <BR> <BR>Though the wheat fields and the clothes lines <BR>And the junkyards and the highways come between us <BR>And some other woman&#39;s cryin&#39; to her mother <BR>&#39;cause she turned and I was gone <BR>I still might run in silence <BR>Tears of joy might stain my face <BR>And the summer sun might burn me till I&#39;m blind <BR>But not to where I cannot see <BR>You walkin&#39; on the back roads <BR>By the rivers flowin&#39; gentle on my mind <BR> <BR>I dip my cup of soup back from a gurglin&#39; cracklin&#39; cauldron <BR>In some train yard <BR>My beard a rustlin&#39; coal pile <BR>And a dirty hat pulled low across my face <BR>Through cupped hands &#39;round a tin can <BR>I pretend to hold you to my breast and find <BR>That you&#39;re waitin&#39; from the back roads <BR>By the rivers of my memory <BR>Ever smilin&#39;, ever gentle on my mind. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42; People if the chill doesn&#39;t run up your back or where ever it goes with this one then it must just be me. The ironic title is one thing but consider: <BR> <BR>THE WORD &#34;BIND&#34;! &#42;&#42;&#42;When I walk along some railroad track&#42;&#42;&#42; Train Yard&#42;&#42;&#42; &#34;And it&#39;s knowin&#39; I&#39;m not shackled <BR>By forgotten words and bonds <BR>And the ink stains that have dried upon some line&#34;&#42;&#42;&#42; &#34;Columns&#34; as in Newspaper columns?&#42;&#42;&#42; Railroad tracks, Rivers, Junkyards, Highways all boundries and all in and around the crime scenes. I&#39;m not sure about Junkyards but I&#39;ll bet there is!&#42;&#42;&#42; And some other woman&#39;s cryin&#39; to her mother <BR>&#39;cause she turned and I was gone <BR>I still might run in silence <BR>Tears of joy might stain my face... &#34;Anna Why Didn&#39;t You Show&#34;???&#42;&#42;&#42; Blindness/eyes&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>Is this too freaking creepy or what?   <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Its Only Make Believe&#42;&#42;&#42;  <BR> <BR>People see us everywhere <BR>They think you really care <BR>But myself I can&#39;t deceive <BR>I know it&#39;s only make believe <BR> <BR>My hopes, my dreams come true, my life I&#39;d give for you, <BR>My heart, a wedding ring, my all, my everything. <BR>My heart I can&#39;t control, you rule my very soul, <BR>My only prayer will be someday you&#39;ll care for me <BR>But it&#39;s o-only make believe. <BR> <BR>My prayer, my hope, and my schemes, you are my every dream <BR>But it&#39;s o-only make believe  <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Murderer speaks of being two himself and a monster&#42;&#42;&#42; Wish to be taken care of/caught?&#42;&#42;&#42;schemes&#42;&#42;&#42;Being seen by people everyday&#42;&#42;&#42;wedding ring? <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;By The Time I Get To Phoenix&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>She&#39;ll find the note I left hangin&#39; on her door <BR> <BR>But she&#39;ll just hear that phone keep on ringin&#39; <BR>Off the wall that&#39;s all <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Note/letter to Anna&#42;&#42;&#42;Shirley Vian&#39;s kids were said to be saved by a phone call&#42;&#42;&#42;phone theme again&#42;&#42;&#42;travel to or from home town&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Country Boy You Got Your Feet In La&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>Livin&#39; in the city <BR>Ain&#39;t never been my idea of gettin&#39; it on <BR>But the job demands that you make new plans <BR>Before your big chance is gone. <BR> <BR>You get a house in the hills. <BR>You&#39;re payin&#39; everyone&#39;s bills <BR>And they tell you that you&#39;re gonna go far <BR>But in the back of my mind, <BR>I hear it time after time, <BR>&#34;Is that who you really are?&#34; <BR> <BR>Country boy, you got your feet in L.A., <BR>But your mind&#39;s on Tennessee. <BR>Lookin&#39; back, I can remember the time <BR>When I sang my songs for free. <BR>Country boy, you got your feet in L.A. <BR>Take a look at everything you own. <BR>But now and then, my heart keeps goin&#39; home. <BR> <BR>Talkin&#39; on the telephone, <BR>Settin&#39; up another day of people to meet. <BR>You&#39;ve gotta do what&#39;s right, <BR>You&#39;ve gotta spend the night, <BR>Stayin&#39; in touch with the street. <BR>When you&#39;re surrounded by friends, <BR>They say the fun never ends, <BR>But I guess I&#39;ll never figure it out <BR>&#39;Cause in the back of my mind, <BR>I hear it time after time, <BR>&#34;Is this what it&#39;s all about?&#34; <BR> <BR>Country boy, you got your feet in L.A., <BR>But your mind&#39;s on Tennessee. <BR>Lookin&#39; back, I can remember the time <BR>When I sang my songs for free. <BR>Country boy, you got your feet in L.A. <BR>Take a look at everything you own. <BR>But now and then, my heart keeps goin&#39; home. <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Feels forced to do something&#42;&#42;&#42;Big Chance&#40;s&#41;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#34;Is that who you really are?&#34;&#42;&#42;&#42;Looking Back/remembering&#42;&#42;&#42; Owns/keeps articles of victims&#42;&#42;&#42; Can live for time without the need but at other times can&#39;t help himself&#42;&#42;&#42; Keeps in touch with victims and crime scene areas/street&#42;&#42;&#42; settin&#39; up&#42;&#42;&#42; &#34;When you&#39;re surrounded by friends, <BR>They say the fun never ends&#34;... A collection of victim photos???&#42;&#42;&#42; Remembers perhaps when he killed for other reason&#40;s&#41;/military? Without pub./fpr free?&#42;&#42;&#42; Theory about living one place and traveling back and forth.&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;THEN YOU CAN TELL ME GOODBYE&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>Kiss me each morning for a million years <BR>Hold me each evening by your side <BR>Tell me you love me for a million years <BR>Then if it don&#39;t work out <BR>Then if it don&#39;t work out <BR>Then you can tell me goodbye <BR> <BR>Sweeten my coffee with a morning kiss <BR>Soften my dreams with your sigh <BR>After you&#39;ve loved me for a million years <BR>Then if it don&#39;t work out <BR>Then if it don&#39;t work out <BR>Then you can tell me goodbye <BR> <BR>If you must go I won&#39;t grieve <BR>If you just wait a life time before you leave <BR>If you must go, I won&#39;t say &#34;no&#34; <BR>Just so we can say that we tried <BR>Tell me you love me for a million years <BR>Then if it don&#39;t work out <BR>Then if it don&#39;t work out <BR>Then you can tell me goodbye  <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Control/Time&#42;&#42;&#42; Lack of grief/sociopath&#42;&#42;&#42; sigh/strangle then revives theory&#42;&#42;&#42; Relives it over &amp; over&#42;&#42;&#42; Coffee/stimulated by act&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Dream Baby &#40;How Long Must I Dream&#41;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR> <BR>Sweet dream baby <BR>Sweet dream baby <BR>Sweet dream baby <BR>How long must I dream <BR> <BR>Dream baby got me dreamin&#39; sweet dreams the whole day through <BR>Dream baby got me dreamin&#39; sweet dreams night time too <BR>I love you and I&#39;m dreaming of you but that won&#39;t do <BR>Dream baby make me stop my dreamin&#39;, you can make my dreams come true. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Baby Photo&#42;&#42;&#42;Make me stop&#42;&#42;&#42;dreams of being stopped/caught?&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Dreams Of The Everyday Housewife&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>The photograph album she takes from the closet and slowly turns the page <BR>And carefully picks up the crumbling flower <BR>The first one he gave her now withered today <BR> <BR>She closes her eyes and touches the house dress that suddenly disappears <BR>And just for the moment she&#39;s wearing the gown <BR>That broke all their minds back so many years <BR> <BR>Oh, such are the dreams of the everyday housewife <BR>You see ev&#39;rywhere any time of the day <BR>An everyday housewife who gave up the good life for me <BR> <BR>Oh, such are the dreams of the everyday housewife <BR>You see ev&#39;rywhere any time of the day <BR>An everyday housewife who gave up the good life for me <BR> <BR>Oh, such are the dreams of the everyday housewife <BR>FADE <BR>You see ev&#39;rywhere any time of the day <BR>An everyday housewife <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Photo Album/slowly turns the pages&#42;&#42;&#42;He enjoys terror of women left at home alone&#42;&#42;&#42;gave up life for him&#42;&#42;&#42;closes her eyes&#42;&#42;&#42;AGAIN stalks victims... sees them&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Galveston&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>Galveston, oh Galveston, I still hear your sea winds blowin&#39; <BR>I still see her dark eyes glowin&#39; <BR>She was 21 when I left Galveston <BR> <BR>Galveston, oh Galveston, I still hear your sea waves crashing <BR>While I watch the cannons flashing <BR>I clean my gun and dream of Galveston <BR> <BR>I still see her standing by the water <BR>Standing there lookin&#39; out to sea <BR>And is she waiting there for me? <BR>On the beach where we used to run <BR> <BR>Galveston, oh Galveston, I am so afraid of dying <BR>Before I dry the tears she&#39;s crying <BR>Before I watch your sea birds flying in the sun <BR>At Galveston, at Galveston <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;Dark Eyes&#42;&#42;&#42;sea birds...Planes? Military?&#42;&#42;&#42;afraid of dying&#42;&#42;&#42;causing tears&#42;&#42;&#42;&#34;Cannon&#34; is a brand of Camera&#42;&#42;&#42;waiting for his return&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>Well... it&#39;s safe to say the Murderer has heard some if not all of these songs but taken out of context are they just a pre-text or is there something here and if so... other clues? Are there anymore clues of past &amp; present and hopfully only in getting caught for the near future? <BR> <BR>You tell me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
