<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1946"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 4:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yeah Juno, <BR> I was thinking as you say about Johnny Cash, that it could be a coinkydink of sorts but when I read Gentle On My Mind &#40;different without the music&#41; I got chills and not the one up the back type but all over a sense of evil. <BR> <BR>As for Glenn writing songs... no doubt but Jimmy Webb wrote Wichita Lineman &amp; By the Time I get to Phoenix <BR> <BR> <BR>Campbell also did a song called &#34;Where&#39;s the Playground Suzie&#34; <BR> <BR>Cousin Susan?&#42;&#42;&#42; Playgrounds and or parks near crime scenes <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
